(project pricklypear-flashcards
 (doc "Pricklypear book chapter: flashcards — decks + spaced-repetition cards as Nopales + data_rows")
 (status implemented)
 (convention ocaml-dune)
 (section flashcards
  
  (doc "Decks, cards, study queue, FSRS-4.5 review, hypermedia UI, agent API")
  (status implemented)
  (verify
   (build "dune build image")
   (smoke "(load-library \"flashcards\") installs flash/… and routes")
   (smoke "GET /flashcards lists decks; create deck appears")
   (smoke "add card to deck; GET deck page lists it")
   (smoke "GET /flashcards/study?deck=… shows due card front; reveal + rate")
   (smoke "rate again/hard/good/easy updates due + stability; card leaves or re-enters queue")
   (smoke "pp_eval '(flash/due)' returns due cards for agents")
   (smoke "seed_stdlib loads flashcards after calendar (or documented order)"))
  (details
   (doc (|
        =========================================================
        PRODUCT INTENT
        =========================================================
        A first-class memorization app on the live image, inspired by:
          - Anki: decks, front/back cards, spaced review grades
          - SuperMemo/FSRS: stability + difficulty + due, scheduled by algorithm
          - Pricklypear: objects in Postgres, UI as Nopales routes,
            agents study/create via eval — no parallel REST API

        NOT a port of Anki desktop.
        NOT file-backed .apkg as the authority (import may come later).
        NOT OCaml system pages — this is a product package (Nopales).

        Killer property: flashcards are Nopales values; agents and humans use the same functions.

        =========================================================
        LAYERING
        =========================================================
        - libs/flashcards/lib.pp  — package flash/… (seed on system/main)
        - data_rows types         — flash-deck, flash-card (shared)
        - Routes via (route …)    — /flashcards and study/edit paths
        - Optional nav entry      — ui/menu pin or seed menu link
        - OCaml                   — only existing CRUD/date prims;
                                    no new kernel prims required for v1
                                    if date-today (calendar) or
                                    string due compares suffice

        =========================================================
        DATA MODEL (v1)
        =========================================================
        Types (deftype on load; fields are documentation + form UI):

        flash-deck
          title          string
          description    string
          color          string (optional CSS token / hex)
          archived       "true" | "" (hide from default list)

        flash-card
          deck_id        uuid string of flash-deck
          front          string (prompt)
          back           string (answer)
          tags           string (comma-separated free text v1)
          suspended      "true" | "" (excluded from study)
          ;; FSRS-4.5 scheduling state (all strings in jsonb v1):
          stability      string float default "0"
          difficulty     string float default "0"
          interval       string int days default "0"
          reps           string int default "0"
          lapses         string int default "0"
          due            string YYYY-MM-DD (empty or past => due now)
          last_reviewed  string YYYY-MM-DD or empty
          created        string YYYY-MM-DD optional

        NO separate flashcard-review log table in v1 (history deferred).
        NO cloze / image occlusion / media blobs in v1.
         NO extra per-type ACL — the RLS floor already isolates rows by
         user (data.u.<user>.* + data.shared.* seed).
        Multi-user isolation of card content is a later multi-user.permissions
        concern, not this chapter's first cut.

        Orphan cards (missing deck_id) show under an "(orphan)" virtual
        deck in the UI; agents can reassign.

        =========================================================
        SRS ALGORITHM (v1 — FSRS-4.5 via kernel prim)
        =========================================================
        Ratings (buttons + flash/review rating arg):
          again | hard | good | easy

        State on each card: stability (float ≥ 0), difficulty (float ≥ 0),
        interval (int days), reps (int), lapses (int), due (YYYY-MM-DD).

        On review with rating R, today = date-today:
          again:
            reps = 0; lapses += 1; interval = 0; due = today
            stability = max(0, stability - 0.2)
          hard:
            interval = max(1, floor(interval * 1.2))
            stability = max(0, stability - 0.15)
            reps += 1; due = today + interval
          good:
            if reps = 0 then interval = 1
            else if reps = 1 then interval = 6
            else interval = floor(interval * stability)
            reps += 1; due = today + interval
          easy:
            if reps = 0 then interval = 4
            else interval = floor(interval * (stability + 1))
            stability = stability + 0.15
            reps += 1; due = today + interval

        New cards: due empty or due <= today, reps=0 → introduce in study.
        Suspended cards never enter the queue.
        Order: due ASC, then session-freshness (last_reviewed < today or
        blank, before last_reviewed == today), then created/id; so a card
        rated Again — due today, last_reviewed today — sinks to the bottom of
        the current stack and is not re-shown until the rest of the due
        batch is cleared. Limit batch (default 20) per study page.

        The core scheduling is delegated to the kernel prim
        (fsrs-schedule stability difficulty elapsed rating) which returns
        (stability' difficulty' interval_days). See libs/flashcards/lib.pp
        flash/apply-rating for the thin Nopales wrapper.

        Date math: reuse calendar/image date prims if present
        (date-today, and a day-add helper). If day-add is missing, file
        issue / add a small flash/add-days using existing prims only —
        do NOT invent a second calendar system.

        =========================================================
        PACKAGE API (flash/ prefix)
        =========================================================
        Decks:
          (flash/decks) -> list of (id . fields)
          (flash/deck id) -> fields | ()
          (flash/deck-create title [description]) -> id
          (flash/deck-update id fields-or-keys…)
          (flash/deck-archive id)

        Cards:
          (flash/cards deck-id [limit]) -> list
          (flash/card id) -> fields | ()
          (flash/add deck-id front back [tags]) -> id
          (flash/update id …)
          (flash/suspend id) / (flash/unsuspend id)
          (flash/delete id)   ; hard delete v1 OK (confirm in UI)

        Study:
          (flash/today) -> "YYYY-MM-DD"
          (flash/due [deck-id] [limit]) -> due cards (not suspended)
          (flash/review id rating) -> updated fields | error string
            rating in again|hard|good|easy
          (flash/stats [deck-id]) -> simple counts
            (due, new, learning, suspended) as printable structure
          (flash/explain front back) -> explanation text from the LLM
            Ask the LLM to explain a card the user doesn't understand.
            Uses agent-session-new with a tutor seed (no tools); returns
            the model's text. Wrapped in an escaped HTML div by the route.

        HTML / routes (handlers are flash/…-page functions):
          (flash/install) or load-side effects:
            (route "/flashcards" "flash/home-page")
            (route "/flashcards/deck" "flash/deck-page")
            (route "/flashcards/study" "flash/study-page")
            (route "/flashcards/explain" "flash/explain-page")
            (route "/flashcards/card" "flash/card-edit-page")  ; optional
          Exact query keys are implementation discretion; document in
          lib.pp header. Prefer ?deck=uuid & ?id=uuid.

        Naming: package directory libs/flashcards/, binding prefix
        flash/ (short, like todo/). Types flash-deck / flash-card
        (not flashcards-deck).

        =========================================================
        HYPERMEDIA UI
        =========================================================
        /flashcards
          - list decks with due counts
          - form: new deck (title)
          - link to study-all (due across decks) optional

        /flashcards/deck?id=
          - deck title, description
          - card table (front truncated, due, stability)
          - add card form (front, back, tags)
          - Study this deck

        /flashcards/study?deck=  (deck optional = all)
          - if no due: empty state + links
          - else one card:
              show FRONT
              [Reveal] → show BACK + rating buttons
          - POST rating → flash/review → redirect next due
          - plain form POST (same as todos); htmx partials optional polish

        /flashcards/explain?id=  (htmx GET, returns an HTML div)
          - reads the card front+back, asks the LLM to explain it in plain
            language, returns an escaped <div> with the explanation.
          - On the study card (after reveal), an Explain button does an htmx
            GET to this route; the response swaps into a #flash-explain div
            below the card. A htmx-indicator span shows Thinking… during the
            request. No tools on the LLM session; no image context needed.

        Mobile-first: big rating buttons, minimal chrome noise.

        Use existing product theme classes (card, btn, table). No new
        OCaml CSS. Optional small flash-local classes in ui/theme later.

        =========================================================
        SEED / NAV
        =========================================================
        - seed_stdlib: load-library "flashcards" after calendar
          (or after todo — order free as long as std/html exists)
        - recipe optional: (load-library "flashcards") from home
        - ui/menu: add Flashcards → /flashcards on system seed when
          easy; personal may pin. Not a kernel nav hard-code.

        =========================================================
        AGENT ACCESS
        =========================================================
        Image is the API:
          python3 scripts/pp_eval.py '(load-library "flashcards")'
          python3 scripts/pp_eval.py '(flash/add deck-id "Q" "A")'
          python3 scripts/pp_eval.py '(flash/due)'
          python3 scripts/pp_eval.py '(flash/review id "good")'
        No flash-specific REST. Bulk import via agent loop over flash/add.

        =========================================================
        NON-GOALS (v1)
        =========================================================
        - Anki .apkg import/export
        - Cloze deletions, image occlusion, audio
        - FSRS / full SM-18
        - Review history graph / heatmap (nice later)
        - Shared multiplayer decks / permissions
        - Sync protocol beyond data_rows + pp_sync package export
        - OCaml system pages for study (package owns UX)
         - Branch-scoped cards (isolation is by user/space/lens, not branch)


   |))
  )
  (subsection model
   (doc "flash-deck + flash-card data_rows; FSRS scheduling fields on card")
   (status implemented)
   (implements libs/flashcards/lib.pp)
   (verify
    (smoke "(deftype …) via load; (flash/add) creates flash-card row")
    (smoke "flash-card has stability difficulty interval reps lapses due fields after review"))

  )
  (subsection srs
   (doc "Nopales scheduler flash/apply-rating; ratings again|hard|good|easy")
   (status implemented)
   (implements libs/flashcards/lib.pp)
   (verify
    (smoke "new card good → due tomorrow or +1 day")
    (smoke "again → due today, lapses+1, ease down")
    (smoke "suspended card not in flash/due"))
  )
  (subsection ui
   (doc "Routes /flashcards, deck, study; form POST ratings")
   (status implemented)
   (implements libs/flashcards/lib.pp)
   (verify
    (smoke "GET /flashcards 200 after load-library")
    (smoke "study POST rating redirects to next or empty"))
  )
  (subsection agent-access
   (doc "pp_eval flash/… as the API")
   (status implemented)
   (verify
    (smoke "pp_eval flash/decks and flash/due"))

  )
 )

)
